      "side": 1,
      "message": "Comment for posterity. There were significant regressions from this CL because of its interaction with the logic that detected clear/discard load ops. When a drawRect was exactly filling the unclipped device, this CL went back to saying it was \"unclipped\" but no longer converted it to a flood-fill so it wasn\u0027t being optimized into a better load op.\n\nThere are however some improvements as well, which are perhaps related to the more general case that the CL comment was referring to. I will try to see if we can easily recover the clear/discard op case w/o having to undo this CL to get the best of both worlds, or I\u0027ll revert this and consider it a worthwhile tradeoff given the improvements with clear/discard ops.",
      "revId": "98e058e5d264b583facfaf55a76c026dfdd04826",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
